WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.971 --> 00:00:18.108
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.881
Okay, new job:
Find something to climb out of here.

00:00:23.881 --> 00:00:25.983
I'm doing a lot of jobs.

00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:28.686
Every employer I've had pulls this crap.

00:00:28.686 --> 00:00:30.354
They hire me to do one thing,

00:00:30.354 --> 00:00:32.990
but what they really mean is one
thing plus fifty other things

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.358
because they don't have enough people.

00:00:34.358 --> 00:00:36.694
And, guess what?  I'm the new hire.

00:00:36.694 --> 00:00:37.728
So, I do it.

00:00:37.728 --> 00:00:38.162
Forever.

00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:39.163
[lock buzzes]

00:00:39.163 --> 00:00:40.731
Right...

00:00:40.731 --> 00:00:43.367
Well, at least Black Mesa
has a legitimate excuse

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.536
that most of their workforce is dead.

00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:47.338
Gotta cover for the dead guys.

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:48.706
Now, what's this say?

00:00:48.706 --> 00:00:52.109
"Superbus Via..."
I don't know much Latin.

00:00:52.109 --> 00:00:54.645
Language of science, my ass.

00:00:54.645 --> 00:00:59.116
It would be kind of cool if I wrote
out "Latin is a dead language" in blood

00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:02.386
and made it look like one of the
soldiers did it as his dying action.

00:01:02.386 --> 00:01:06.757
People would say, "Wow, those were
his last words, huh?" Make them think.

00:01:06.757 --> 00:01:11.195
Hm. I guess I could stack these bodies
to make a human staircase out of here.

00:01:11.195 --> 00:01:13.230
But, that's going to be a lot of hauling.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.033
I'd probably need at least five or six.

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:17.501
They're heavy, too.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:19.937
I'd wear myself out
if I moved all of them.

00:01:19.937 --> 00:01:22.873
I'm sure there's a cheap lab
stool around here somewhere.

00:01:22.873 --> 00:01:24.041
[explosion-like sound]

00:01:24.041 --> 00:01:24.775
What was that?

00:01:25.743 --> 00:01:27.578
I don't like hearing explosions
if I'm not the one

00:01:27.578 --> 00:01:28.112
[door hisses]
making--

00:01:28.112 --> 00:01:29.213
God, Jesus...!

00:01:29.213 --> 00:01:31.148
Frickin' door conspiracy!

00:01:31.148 --> 00:01:32.716
You can't tell me there isn't one.

00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:34.218
They know...

00:01:34.785 --> 00:01:35.853
Hey, a button!

00:01:35.853 --> 00:01:38.689
I've got my button-pressing
gloves on and I'll--wait...

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:40.391
Wait... wait....

00:01:40.391 --> 00:01:42.860
Maybe I shouldn't press THIS button.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.862
I'm getting some weird vibes here.

00:01:44.862 --> 00:01:47.498
Like, why is there a dead guy
inside these cages?

00:01:47.498 --> 00:01:50.868
I don't know what department
this is, but this isn't how we kept our lab.

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:55.339
If someone turned up dead in one of our
experiments, it got cleaned up immediately.

00:01:55.339 --> 00:01:56.907
I'm not going to press that
button.

00:01:56.907 --> 00:02:00.044
I'm going to press THIS bu--
no, maybe I shouldn't.

00:02:00.044 --> 00:02:01.679
I'm having déjà vu.

00:02:01.679 --> 00:02:03.447
I've been in this room before.

00:02:03.447 --> 00:02:07.084
The last time I pressed that
button, I remember a white hot light

00:02:07.084 --> 00:02:09.753
and then the universe felt just
a little bit emptier.

00:02:10.354 --> 00:02:12.022
We shouldn't be making these buttons.

00:02:13.557 --> 00:02:14.692
Whoa-ho-ho-ho!

00:02:15.359 --> 00:02:17.161
It's that time of the year again.

00:02:17.995 --> 00:02:19.029
Okay...

00:02:20.297 --> 00:02:21.565
TAG!  YOU'RE IT!

00:02:21.565 --> 00:02:23.434
HECU: We've got Freeman!
NOT YOU, THE OTHER GUY!

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.536
YOU'RE IT!  YOU'RE IT!  YOU'RE IT!

00:02:25.536 --> 00:02:26.670
RRRRR!

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.771
No tag-backs.

00:02:28.639 --> 00:02:28.973
[hic]

00:02:29.273 --> 00:02:31.642
Oh, nice.  I have the hiccups.

00:02:31.642 --> 00:02:34.545
Man, I get really nervous
after killing people.

00:02:34.545 --> 00:02:35.579
Is that normal?

00:02:35.579 --> 00:02:38.215
I think it's because there
could be other people to kill

00:02:38.215 --> 00:02:41.018
and I never really know if my job's done.

00:02:41.018 --> 00:02:41.218
[hic]

00:02:41.218 --> 00:02:42.219
[alien grunt growls]

00:02:42.219 --> 00:02:43.387
CLEARLY IT ISN'T!

00:02:43.387 --> 00:02:45.189
THAT'S A PRETTY BIG
OVERSIGHT IF I'M TRYING--

00:02:47.558 --> 00:02:50.094
WHY IS IT MY JOB TO KILL
EVERYONE?!

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:55.566
I almost feel like my degree
is being wasted here.

00:02:55.566 --> 00:02:58.569
I mean, what I'm doing now
really has nothing to do with

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:01.138
quantum mechanics or general relativity.

00:03:01.138 --> 00:03:02.539
There's just no crossover.

00:03:03.741 --> 00:03:05.009
Don't come near me!

00:03:05.676 --> 00:03:06.977
Don't come near me!

00:03:07.244 --> 00:03:08.612
No!  NO!

00:03:08.612 --> 00:03:11.415
I HAVE A PERSONAL SPACE ZONE, GOD DAMMIT!

00:03:11.415 --> 00:03:12.483
PERSONAL SPACE!

00:03:12.716 --> 00:03:12.950
[hic]

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.052
Nobody has any respect for my privacy!

00:03:15.052 --> 00:03:16.787
They all think I've done something!

00:03:16.787 --> 00:03:18.522
[gibbering]

00:03:18.522 --> 00:03:19.423
Out of ammo, okay!

00:03:19.423 --> 00:03:20.858
Sorry!  Sorry about that!

00:03:20.858 --> 00:03:22.059
Thought you were somebody else.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:23.861
Did he buy that?

00:03:24.361 --> 00:03:26.430
[gibbering]
I would--I don't...I don't know.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.965
Maybe he respects my privacy.

00:03:27.965 --> 00:03:30.601
I mean, there is no
actual RIGHT to privacy,

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:34.838
but it's implied by the rest of
the Constitution... and this gun.

00:03:35.539 --> 00:03:36.740
What's going on here?

00:03:37.808 --> 00:03:38.542
[lock buzzes]

00:03:38.542 --> 00:03:42.079
It's a prototype
cheese slicer, I guess.

00:03:42.079 --> 00:03:43.914
Doesn't look like it's going too well.

00:03:43.914 --> 00:03:45.783
Okay, where is this guy?

00:03:45.783 --> 00:03:48.719
I can't have somebody sneakier
than I am running around here.

00:03:48.719 --> 00:03:50.554
Then the whole system falls apart.

00:03:52.189 --> 00:03:53.557
Oh, I think I got him.

00:03:53.557 --> 00:03:54.625
Yeah, that's right.

00:03:54.625 --> 00:03:55.092
[hic]

00:03:55.092 --> 00:03:59.163
Thought you could take cover in this
completely empty hallway with nothing in it.

00:03:59.163 --> 00:04:03.100
And the door opens so that means
you weren't trying to run away.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.202
So, that really was your plan.

00:04:05.202 --> 00:04:07.805
Well, you're not going to make
sergeant like that.

00:04:07.805 --> 00:04:10.407
So, looks like I've
gone in circles again.

00:04:10.407 --> 00:04:13.410
But now, I can do it on the next floor!

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.312
I can't wait; I'm going to run up there.

00:04:15.312 --> 00:04:16.480
[gunfire in distance]

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:16.880
[hic]

00:04:17.114 --> 00:04:19.316
OKAY, I NEED EVERYBODY TO CALM DOWN!

00:04:19.316 --> 00:04:20.651
JUST CALM DOWN!

00:04:20.651 --> 00:04:23.220
I CAN'T HELP ANYONE IF YOU'RE NOT CALM!

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.488
ARE WE CALM YET?!

00:04:24.488 --> 00:04:24.955
YES?!

00:04:24.955 --> 00:04:25.322
NO?!

00:04:25.322 --> 00:04:26.457
OH-OH MY GOD!

00:04:27.758 --> 00:04:28.692
WE NEED TO RELAX!

00:04:28.692 --> 00:04:29.760
YOU'RE NOT RELAXED!

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.328
JESUS CHRIST!

00:04:31.328 --> 00:04:31.929
Aaaahhh....

00:04:31.929 --> 00:04:35.766
This session's off to a rocky start, but
I think I just need to change tactics.

00:04:35.766 --> 00:04:37.034
OKAY, LISTEN UP EVERYBODY!

00:04:37.034 --> 00:04:37.968
ARE WE CALM?!

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:40.304
RELAX AND FOLLOW THE SOUND OF MY VOICE!

00:04:40.304 --> 00:04:42.039
I NEED YOU TO TAKE DEEP BREATHS!

00:04:42.039 --> 00:04:43.340
DEEP BREATHS!

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.508
YES, THAT'S GOOD!

00:04:44.508 --> 00:04:46.777
NO!  NOT LIKE THAT!  START OVER!

00:04:47.311 --> 00:04:47.644
[hic]

00:04:48.045 --> 00:04:50.347
Actually, I think that's all the
time we have for today.

00:04:50.347 --> 00:04:51.615
We'll meet again next week.

00:04:52.616 --> 00:04:56.153
Okay, now that everyone's calmed
down, we can start thinking rationally.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.889
It stands to reason that
with so many of you here,

00:04:58.889 --> 00:05:00.290
there must be a functional entrance.

00:05:00.691 --> 00:05:01.024
[hic]

00:05:01.425 --> 00:05:03.727
Unless I'm imagining everyone here.

00:05:03.727 --> 00:05:05.462
That would be a game changer.

00:05:05.462 --> 00:05:05.996
Hey...

00:05:05.996 --> 00:05:06.530
[laser blasts, whines]

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.898
[laser blasts, whines]
Whoa!

00:05:07.898 --> 00:05:09.266
That's awesome.

00:05:09.266 --> 00:05:11.468
I'm going to leave this on.
It looks expensive.

00:05:12.703 --> 00:05:14.905
Hm, that is something to think about.

00:05:14.905 --> 00:05:18.242
If I am imagining all these soldiers,
then I'm just shooting random people.

00:05:18.242 --> 00:05:20.010
Or maybe nobody at all.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.379
But, if that's the case,
then it make sense why--

00:05:22.379 --> 00:05:22.613
[hic]

00:05:23.013 --> 00:05:24.381
--people are trying to kill me.

00:05:25.182 --> 00:05:25.649
[houndeyes squeal, charge up]

00:05:25.649 --> 00:05:28.018
Dammit, not you!
You're not even people!

00:05:28.018 --> 00:05:28.752
Wuaaah!

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.188
Bouncing nightmares...

00:05:31.188 --> 00:05:31.722
[hic]
[houndeyes charge up]

00:05:33.557 --> 00:05:37.661
IF I WANT YOU LITTLE SPACE MAGGOTS
JUMPING AT MY FACE, I'LL ASK FOR IT!

00:05:37.661 --> 00:05:39.463
AND I'M NEVER GOING TO ASK FOR THAT!

00:05:39.463 --> 00:05:41.031
[laser blasts, whines]

00:05:41.031 --> 00:05:43.133
Well, lasers make me happy.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:44.635
Maybe not as much food,

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:46.036
some painkillers,

00:05:46.036 --> 00:05:46.870
bed rest,

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.572
not being persecuted,

00:05:48.572 --> 00:05:50.674
just getting my life
back on track in general.

00:05:50.674 --> 00:05:52.409
But, hey, I'll take lasers.

00:05:52.409 --> 00:05:54.311
GUARD: What is this thing?
Some-some kind of weapon?

00:05:54.311 --> 00:05:56.146
SCIENTIST: Put that down. It's a prototype.

00:05:56.146 --> 00:05:57.314
I'm hearing voices again.

00:05:57.314 --> 00:05:58.682
[tau cannon blast]
What?

00:05:58.682 --> 00:06:00.117
GUARD: Why aren't we using it?

00:06:00.117 --> 00:06:02.419
SCIENTIST: It's much too unpredictable.

00:06:02.419 --> 00:06:03.387
SCIENTIST: Don't let it overcharge!

00:06:03.387 --> 00:06:04.488
GUARD: What-what do you mean, "Over--"

00:06:04.488 --> 00:06:05.889
[tau cannon explosion]
[gasps]

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:11.495
You know, for every mistake I make,
somebody else is making an even bigger one.

00:06:12.129 --> 00:06:14.064
Yuck. Well, I'm not touching that thing.

00:06:14.064 --> 00:06:16.233
I doubt it's any safer
with blood all over it.

00:06:16.233 --> 00:06:17.668
[laser blast, whines]

00:06:17.668 --> 00:06:19.336
Hey, how did those guys get in here?

00:06:19.336 --> 00:06:20.837
Oh, of course.  Through the ceiling.

00:06:21.405 --> 00:06:22.339
I guess they blew up--

00:06:22.339 --> 00:06:22.606
[hic]

00:06:22.906 --> 00:06:24.808
--the rope they used to get in there.

00:06:24.808 --> 00:06:27.878
I guess I'm getting jaded in that
seeing some body parts lying around

00:06:27.878 --> 00:06:30.080
doesn't freak me out the way it used to.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.049
It still freaks out most people.

00:06:32.049 --> 00:06:33.050
A lot.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.152
Like, if we're able to cl--
oh, hey, a button!

00:06:35.886 --> 00:06:37.454
[button clicks]
[growls]

00:06:37.454 --> 00:06:39.223
Damn, I don't think it has any power.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:42.526
But, yeah, if we were able to
clone body parts easily,

00:06:42.526 --> 00:06:44.528
I'd just want to sprinkle them
across the countryside

00:06:44.528 --> 00:06:47.064
and covertly videotape people
discovering them.

00:06:47.064 --> 00:06:49.633
Small towns where not a lot
happens would be best.

00:06:49.633 --> 00:06:50.167
Just leave--

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:50.434
[hic]

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:53.170
Just leave a severed arm
lying there on Main Street.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:55.539
Especially if they don't know it's cloned.

00:06:55.539 --> 00:06:57.741
Wait, I've already been here.
Christ...

00:06:57.741 --> 00:07:01.278
So, then a week later, I'd come back and
leave a cloned leg there that's just as fresh

00:07:01.278 --> 00:07:03.814
so that they think I'm hacking
up some guy in my basement.

00:07:03.814 --> 00:07:06.116
People would worry over nothing.
It'd be great.

00:07:06.116 --> 00:07:07.351
[laser blast, whines]

00:07:07.351 --> 00:07:09.386
More lasers.  Fuck yeah!

00:07:09.386 --> 00:07:13.490
Maybe if I turn all these on and redirect them,
I could start shooting down the satellites.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.925
That would be so rad.

00:07:14.925 --> 00:07:17.828
Oooh!  I can feel the hum off this thing!

00:07:17.828 --> 00:07:18.662
Let's try again!

00:07:18.662 --> 00:07:19.363
[machine powering up]

00:07:19.363 --> 00:07:20.163
Oh-ho-ho!

00:07:21.231 --> 00:07:22.099
[high pitched whine]

00:07:22.099 --> 00:07:23.467
Bad ass!

00:07:24.835 --> 00:07:25.969
Bad ass!

00:07:28.772 --> 00:07:29.873
Oh yeah!

00:07:29.873 --> 00:07:33.243
Once I reorient this thing, I
can shoot a satellite down for sure.

00:07:33.243 --> 00:07:34.578
[doors open, computer chirps]

00:07:34.578 --> 00:07:37.481
Somebody's going to be missing
their TV channels tonight.

00:07:37.848 --> 00:07:38.334
[hic]

